{"name":"Cracker Crumbs","hex":"#d3b9b0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cracker","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A noisy boaster; a swaggering fellow.","A dry, thin, crispy baked bread (usually salty or savoury, but sometimes sweet, as in the case of graham crackers and animal crackers)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cracker"},{"term":"crumbs","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of crumb"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of crumb"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crumbs"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cracker (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Cracker is an American rock band formed in 1990 by lead singer David Lowery and guitarist Johnny Hickman. The band's first album Cracker was released in 1992 on Virgin Records; it included the single \"Teen Angst \", which went to No. 1 on the U.S. Modern Rock chart. The band's follow-up, the 1993 album Kerosene Hat included the hit songs \"Low\", \"Get Off This\" and \"Euro-Trash Girl\". Cracker has released nine studio albums and several compilations, collaborations, solo projects and live albums. The band mix influences and sounds from rock, punk, grunge, psychedelia, country, blues and folk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/CrackerJonesBeach.jpg/330px-CrackerJonesBeach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cracker_(band)"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"cracker":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4b/En-au-cracker.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/4b/En-au-cracker.ogg/En-au-cracker.ogg.mp3"}],"crumbs":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/En-us-crumbs.ogg